  "worked_solution": "The vector equation of the straight line passing through $M$ and parallel to $v$ is given by\n\n$$\nr=m+tv,\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )$ and $m$ is the position vector of $M.$ \n\nWe can find a direction vector by computing the displacement vector between the given points $M(0,1,0)$ and $N(3,4,-1)$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\overset{\\to }{MN} \\\\  & =\u27e83,4,-1\u27e9-\u27e80,1,0\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e83,3,-1\u27e9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the vector equation of the line is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
